n more  because she had two  completely legitimate workable i was  good with them  send-offs she had one at the end of  death in heaven  i would have been completely fine with  that being her last appearance it would  have been fine  and i would have been fine with this one  being her last appearance up  until the very very end because the  whole episode deals with  dreams within dreams yes it gets a bit  inceptiony it's it's basically inception  meets alien so there's all that stuff  but  where it should have ended there was one  wake up to many  when the doctor goes to get the crab off  of clara's face and find her  62 years later from the last time he saw  her and she's just  she's lived her life it was bittersweet  it was a little sad but it felt  right it felt fitting it should have  ended there but then he wakes up  one more time goes to her she's still  that young clara  that we've always known and he rescues  her and now they go off together and  we're going to get  a whole other series with clara and it's  actually even more irritating because  they give  danny pink a great last sort of  secondary send-off in this as well  which just sort of emphasizes how good  clara is with  him but he's dead i suppose i i will add  a slight ass for a song to this i  suppose it's possible they're going to  find some ridiculous way to bring him  back because they still haven't really  resolved the fact that we saw  what was very clearly their descendant  in listen and he's  in the future i don't know if that's  just going to get dropped and sort of  chalked up to the whole well the  timeline got changed i guess that guy  doesn't exist anymore or if they're  actually going to reconcile that which  would  potentially involve bringing danny back  somehow i god i really hope not though  up until that very end i i thought this  was a wonderful episode i thought it was  fun it was touching it was scary  it was twisty once you realized that we  were dealing with dreams  seeing wh